  "notes": "Arduino Severino S3v3 user-manual page. Digital labels use board names D0-D13 / A0-A5 derived from the printed PORT B(D8-D13), PORT D(D0-D7), PORT C(A0-A5) captions, with the silkscreen number first in functions. PWM brackets cover 11/10/9 (PWM) and 6/5/3 ('(PWM-AT168)'). Power header '0' pins are printed as 0 (0V). Skipped: X1 DE-9 serial connector (only pin numbers 1/5/6/9 printed, no names), DC1 power jack, jumpers JP0 (1-2-3, PIN 0/1 vs SERIAL ENABLE) and JP4 (AUTO RESET ENABLE), switch S1, LEDs."
